  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Inspect and decode local CAN DBC and capture-log files. Every tool is read-only, files remain on the local machine, and list outputs are bounded. For signal-availability questions, make one bounded log_signal_inventory call first, before any lower-level tool calls. Treat DBC and capture-log inputs as immutable: never rewrite, clean, normalize, or copy them to work around parsing problems. Surface parse_diagnostics, identify messages where decode_safe is false, and continue reporting results from safe messages. If an error has retryable: false, relay its code, message, and recommended_action, then stop; do not fall back to shell commands or ad hoc Python.",
